From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: WWWorm <noreply@localhost>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 11:26:29 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Add AMD FidelityFX upscaling and frame generation on Vulkan

Loads the FSR SDK 2.4.0 ffx-api runtime (hash-checked) next to the
executable and drives FSR 3.1/FSR 4 upscaling from the forward clustered
renderer as Viewport.SCALING_3D_MODE_FSR_SDK. Upscaling needs no
presentation owner. With the startup owner "amd" FidelityFX becomes the
graphics SDK owner: it asks for its present, async compute and image
acquire queues, enables subgroup size control and synchronization2, and
replaces the swapchain so Viewport.frame_generation runs FSR frame
generation. With DLSS the same flag belongs to DLSS-G.

The temporal scene shader preparation is shared with DLSS, FSR 2 and TAA.
Exposed to scripts through the FidelityFX singleton. Enabled with
use_fsr_sdk=yes on Windows Vulkan builds.
